{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_66hbjpjzz4gbpbytguiqibcfirhvwkthmhbgm4pbfyafzyezpk3q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the C linear algebra library to safe, idiomatic Rust by implementing every `unimplemented!()` body across the four source files:\n\n- **`src/utils.rs`** — `exclusive_or`, `roundn`, `custom_assert`, `print_call_stack`\n- **`src/vector.rs`** — All vector operations (creation, fill, copy, arithmetic, magnitude, dot/cross product, distance, etc.)\n- **`src/matrix.rs`** — All matrix operations (creation, accessors, diagonals, transpose, multiply, sub-matrix, minors, cofactors, adjugate, LU decomposition, determinant, inverse, geometric transforms)\n- **`src/linear_algebra.rs`** — The public-facing wrapper functions that call into the `_impl` functions from `matrix.rs` / `vector.rs`\n\n### Key correctness notes\n1. **`pivot_matrix` swap-count bug**: The C code has `swaps++` on the `int*` parameter, which increments the pointer rather than the pointed-to value. The C version always returns 0 swaps. I mirrored this exactly so `determinant` (which uses `pow(-1, swaps-1) = -1`) produces the same numerical results — needed to pass the 4×4 determinant test.\n2. **`multiply_matrices` square-only restriction**: Mirrors the C requirement that `m->cols == n->cols && m->rows == n->rows`.\n3. **`has_zero_col` index swap**: Mirrors the apparent C bug where the inner/outer loop bounds use `rows`/`cols` swapped.\n4. No `unsafe`, no FFI/`libc`. Pure safe Rust with `Vec<f64>` for storage.\n\n### Test results\nAll 24 tests pass under `timeout 60 cargo test`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":354,"cache_read_input_tokens":87062,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":354,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standa